# ORCA 3D Model Assets
#
# This directory hosts the GLB/GLTF model assets loaded by the
# React Three Fiber components in `src/components/3d/`.
#
# Expected assets (create or drop in as they become available):
#
#   orca.glb              — flagship orca model
#   cargo-ship.glb        — bulk/container cargo vessel
#   tanker.glb            — oil/chemical tanker
#   fishing-boat.glb      — commercial fishing vessel
#   passenger-ship.glb    — ferry / cruise vessel
#   research-vessel.glb   — oceanographic research vessel
#   tug-boat.glb          — harbor tug
#   pleasure-craft.glb    — yacht / sailboat
#   military-ship.glb     — patrol vessel
#   satellite.glb         — Earth observation satellite
#   buoy.glb              — oceanographic buoy
#   underwater-sensor.glb — moored subsurface sensor
#   submarine.glb         — AUV / submarine
#   marine-drone.glb      — aerial/surface hybrid drone
#   earth.glb             — high-fidelity Earth (optional)
#
# Recommended pipeline:
#   - Blender export → glTF 2.0 Binary (.glb)
#   - Draco mesh compression ON
#   - KTX2 texture compression ON
#   - Y-up, meters, centered at origin
#   - Max 1 material per mesh where possible
#
# The components in `src/components/3d/` already accept a `url` prop.
# When a GLB is available, simply pass the path and the procedural
# fallback will be replaced with the loaded model automatically.